#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

cat <<'USAGE'
siril-stretch helper wrapper

This is a local helper entrypoint for the siril-stretch skill.
It documents the intended orchestration model:

  1. Analyze input image and histogram.
  2. Produce 3 full GHS→BP candidates for the round.
  3. Perform technical analysis.
  4. Perform exact-path visual review.
  5. Select round winner.
  6. Repeat for another round if justified.
  7. Stop after a minimum of 2 rounds and maximum of 5 rounds.
  8. Prepare final 3-candidate review from preserved round winners.

Recommended autonomous prompt:
  Process <project name> with stretch

This wrapper is intentionally lightweight; Siril transformations should be executed
through the companion scripts in scripts/.
USAGE
